  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A Uniform rod <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></math> is hinged at its end <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>&nbsp;and the other end of the rod is connected to a block through a massless string as shown in the figure. The pulley is smooth and massless. Masses of the block and the rod are same and are equal to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi></math>. The&nbsp;acceleration of the block just after the release from this position is<br />\r<br />\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\qt0004_e5e33b53c98b.jpeg\" style=\"width: 240px; height: 188px;\" /></p>\r"
  },
